descriptions:
Improve access to climate resilient water and improved sanitation services and good hygiene practices for 1.2 million people in the prioritised drought affected and drought prone areas of Ethiopia. 
The Programme aims to realise this through a combination of targeted Financial Aid and Technical Assistance support. The FA will focus primarily on implementing climate resilient WaSH facilities which ensure year round access to resilient WaSH services at household, community and institution level in the targeted intervention areas. This will be complemented with TA support that focuses on: 
•Strengthening the WaSH delivery systems of selected rural multi-village management units and urban utilities in the Climate Resilient WaSH (CR WaSH) intervention areas to improve their operational efficiency and be self-sustained entities. This includes support to women and youth groups to engage in spare part supply and service maintenance;
•Formulating a sustainable financing strategy for the WaSH sector with a focus on domestic revenue streams and mobilizing private capital;
•Tailored TA to selected Developing Regional States (DRS); 
•Piloting innovations to build the private sector supply; and, 
•Deep Dive Learning Evaluation for continued adaptive learning.  Capturing and utilizing evidence of what works to inform better delivery through adaptive learning.

The Programme targets primarily drought prone, drought affected and hard to reach areas and will implement social targeting to better address the needs of women and girls and people with disabilities through inclusive WaSH service provision.  Overall the programme through its complementary components (FA + TA) will address issues related to sustainable WaSH services, and greater equity in service provision, whilst offering high value for money and a clear rationale for continued investment.

This Technical Assistance (TA) will complement the Financial Assistance channeled through the OWNP Consolidated WaSH Account (OWNP/CWA) and will focus on strengthening systems, which are the key determinants of sustainability of the service delivery.
The Financial Aid will be complemented with TA support that focuses on: 
•Strengthening the WaSH service delivery systems of selected rural multi-village management units and urban utilities in the Climate Resilient WaSH (CR WaSH) intervention areas to improve their operational efficiency and be self-sustained entities. This includes support to women and youth groups to engage in spare part supply and service maintenance;
•Formulating a sustainable financing strategy for the WaSH sector with a focus on domestic revenue streams and mobilising private capital;
•Tailored TA to selected drought prone SCRS-WaSH regions;
•Piloting innovations to build the private sector supply; and, 
•Deep Dive Learning Evaluation for continued adaptive learning.
